  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "The strongest finding so far is the ~13% accuracy jump from adding multiprofile+avgpool to the RNA-only scVI setting (config_005: 0.650 vs. config_004: 0.520). The second strongest finding is that multimodal concat fusion with ResNet-50 adds a modest but consistent gain over RNA-only (config_028: 0.536 vs. config_004: 0.520). The critical open question is whether these two gains are additive: does the multiprofile aggregation benefit transfer to the multimodal setting? config_030 (multimodal, multiprofile, scVI_n200, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) is the direct logical extension of both config_005 (adding the validated image modality) and config_028 (adding multiprofile+avgpool), testing one conceptual question from each parent. If the gains are additive, this could yield a configuration well above 0.65, establishing a new strong baseline. If they are not additive, we learn an important interaction constraint that would redirect subsequent experiments toward optimizing within the multiprofile RNA-only space rather than pursuing multimodal combinations. Under a limited budget, exploiting the single largest observed effect (multiprofile) in the most promising direction (multimodal, already validated) is the highest-information next step."
}

